{
  "id": "V13",
  "title": "Window between two solid walls",
  "intent": "A window is modelled as two solid (segmented) walls with a 4 ft gap — the tool rule since 2026-09-29: segmented walls never have openings. Checks the gravity statics of each wall with an off-centre point load (unequal end reactions), the end forces at both ends in both directions, and that the load over the window is reported as not carried.",
  "covers": [
    "Segmented walls are solid (openings only on FTAO)",
    "Gravity end reactions by statics (R_R = Σ P·x̄ / L)",
    "Unequal ends → different T / C each end",
    "gravity_unsupported over the gap"
  ],
  "handCalc": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "text": "Story shear V = 6 k to two equal 6 ft walls → 3.00 k each; v = 0.7 × 3000 / 6 = 350.00 plf → 6\" o.c. 312 < 349.99999999999994 NG → 4\" o.c. (470), D/C 0.745. h/b = 10/6 = 1.67 ≤ 2. N_E = 3 × 10 / 6 = ±5.00 k."
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "text": "SW-11 (0–6 ft) D pieces: uniform 200 × 6 = 1.20 k at 3.0; point 2 k at 1.5; self 10 × 6 × 10 = 0.60 k at 3.0 → D = 3.80 k."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "text": "SW-11 R_R = (1.20 × 3 + 2 × 1.5 + 0.60 × 3) / 6 = 1.400 k; R_L = 3.80 − 1.400 = 2.400 k. Live L = 100 × 6 = 0.60 k → 0.30 k per end."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "text": "SW-11 left end: T (→, (0.6 − 0.14S_DS)D + 0.7E) = 0.7 × 5.00 − 0.46 × 2.400 = 2.396 k; C (←) = 1.14 × 2.400 + 0.7 × 5.00 = 6.236 k (combo (6) 5.502 k)."
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "text": "SW-11 right end: T (←) = 0.7 × 5.00 − 0.46 × 1.400 = 2.856 k; C (→) = 1.14 × 1.400 + 0.7 × 5.00 = 5.096 k."
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "text": "SW-12 (10–16 ft): D = 1.20 + 0.60 = 1.80 k → 0.90 k per end; T = 0.7 × 5.00 − 0.46 × 0.90 = 3.086 k; C = 1.14 × 0.90 + 0.7 × 5.00 = 4.526 k."
    },
    {
      "step": 7,
      "text": "Hardware: SW-11 left T 2.396 k → HDUE3; SW-12 T 3.086 k → HDUE3. SW-11 left post for C 6.236 k at 10 ft ((2)2x4 minimum): (2)2x4 cap 5.00 k < C → (3)2x4 (cap 7.50 k)."
    },
    {
      "step": 8,
      "text": "The uniform load over the window (6–10 ft) has nothing below: D 0.80 k and L 0.40 k not carried (audit note, excluded in G4 / G8) → G1–G12 pass."
    },
    {
      "step": 9,
      "text": "Eq. 4.3-1 per wall at 1.0E (lateral only, gravity does not enter): SW-12 (Eq. 4.3-1, → governs): v = 1000 × 3.000 / 6 = 500.00 plf, A = 10.5 in², G_a = 20 k/in → 8vh³/(EAb) = 0.0373; vh/(1000G_a) = 0.2500; Δ_HD = 0.127 × 5000.00 / 3790 (ASD cap) = 0.1675 (HDUE3, T = 5000.00 lb); r = 5000.00 / (10.5 × 625) = 0.7619 → Δ_c = 0.0224; h·Δa/b = 10 × (0.1675 + 0.0224) / 6 = 0.3165 → δ = 0.6039 in."
    },
    {
      "step": 10,
      "text": "Story drift Level 1: δxe = the largest wall δ = SW-12 0.6039 in → δx = Cd·δxe/Ie = 4 × 0.6039 / 1.0 = 2.415 in vs Δa = 0.020 × 10 × 12 = 2.400 in → NG — over the limit (design pinned, so drift sizing does not change it; the line reports drift NG)."
    }
